  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_034 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.715 acc, driven primarily by the scvi_n200 RNA encoder. The key open question is whether the aggregation method over multiple profiles can further improve performance with this much richer representation. With the weaker scgpt encoder, avgpool marginally beat transformer (0.518 vs 0.507), but that gap was small and may not hold with scvi_n200's higher-dimensional, more structured embeddings where inter-profile interactions might be better captured by a transformer. config_008 changes only the aggregation (avgpool → transformer) while holding all other settings identical to config_034, giving a clean single-variable comparison. This is the best use of the next experiment because it directly exploits the strongest evidence while isolating the effect of aggregation, which is a critical architectural choice for multiprofile models and could unlock further gains or confirm that simple averaging is sufficient."
}

